{"name":"Persuasion","hex":"#c4ae96","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"persuasion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of persuading, or trying to do so; the addressing of arguments to someone with the intention of changing their mind or convincing them of a certain point of view, course of action etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An argument or other statement intended to influence one's opinions or beliefs; a way of persuading someone. \n\n All activity attempting to influence or control others' behavior or profession of beliefs, from convincing to threatening, assault, or battery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persuasion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Persuasion","blocks":[{"text":"Persuasion is the act of influencing a person's beliefs, attitudes, intentions, motivations, or behavior. Research on persuasion and its affects is of interest to many fields, and is a frequent topic in the specialty of social psychology. Persuasion usually affects the decision making of an individual, and it is aimed at a variety of groups, including consumers, voters, and others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Gnome-network-wireless.svg/330px-Gnome-network-wireless.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persuasion","wikidata":"Q1231428"},{"title":"Persuasion (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Persuasion is the last novel completed by the English author Jane Austen. It was published with Northanger Abbey on 20 December 1817, six months after her death, although the title page is dated 1818."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/NorthangerPersuasionTitlePage.jpg/330px-NorthangerPersuasionTitlePage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persuasion_(novel)","wikidata":"Q333179"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thu